/Users/tiger/.codex/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/capabilities/automation.md:13:The exact rule shape requires `key`, `name`, `object_key`, `enabled`, object-valued `trigger`, and a non-empty `instructions` array. Put `phase` and `operation` inside `trigger`; do not author top-level `phase` or `event`. Each instruction requires `key` and `type`. Supported types are `assert`, `derive_fields`, `emit_event`, `invoke_business_action`, and `start_workflow`; `audit` is not an instruction type. Before-persistence rules may use only synchronous guard/derive semantics. After-persistence rules may invoke an Action, start a Workflow, or emit an event. `invoke_business_action` requires `config.action_key`; `start_workflow` requires `config.workflow_key`.
